</element-citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>L&#x000f6;ck</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Perrin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Seidlitz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Residual tumour hypoxia in head-and-neck cancer patients undergoing primary radiochemotherapy, final results of a prospective trial on repeat FMISO-PET imaging</article-title><source>Radiother Oncol</source><year>2017</year><volume>124</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>540</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.radonc.2017.08.010</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">28843726</pub-id>
